From: OpenWrt EHR330 support <openwrt-devel@lists.openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: fw-dec: forward last-block flag

Newer MediaTek firmware decryption implementations process images in chunks
and use x3 to identify the final AES-CBC block. Forward that argument from
the existing SIP wrapper.

---
 plat/mediatek/apsoc_common/bl31/apsoc_sip_svc_common.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/plat/mediatek/apsoc_common/bl31/apsoc_sip_svc_common.c
+++ b/plat/mediatek/apsoc_common/bl31/apsoc_sip_svc_common.c
@@ -236,7 +236,7 @@ static uintptr_t apsoc_sip_fw_dec_image(
 {
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	ret = fw_dec_image(x1, x2);
+	ret = fw_dec_image(x1, x2, x3);
 	SMC_RET1(handle, ret);
 }
 #endif /* MTK_FW_ENC_VIA_BL31 */
